/** @page uuidreleasenotesguide Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section uuid_v_1_4_2 Version 1.4.2

    <b>Bug Fixes</b>
    - fixed Windows isNull() implementation to return correct result instead of RPC status
    - fixed Windows compare() implementation to return comparison result instead of RPC status
    - fixed memory leak in static UUID::get() for OSSP UUID library
    - fixed configure macro mismatch (HAS_UUID_UNPARSE_CASE -> HAVE_UUID_UNPARSE_CASE)
    - fixed UUID generation flag values to use proper bit flags (QUF_RANDOM, QUF_TIME, QUF_EMPTY were
      not powers of 2, causing UUID::Empty and other flags to not work correctly)
    - fixed the code flags on static UUID::get(), which declared the method free of side effects; each
      call generates a new UUID and consumes entropy, so discarding the return value is observable,
      but the parser reported that such a call had no effect

    <b>Other Changes</b>
    - updated minimum %Qore version requirement to 0.9
    - improved test coverage with negative tests and corner cases
    - updated GitLab CI configuration to use k8s runner tag
    - updated GitHub organization references in CI

    @section uuid_v_1_4_1 Version 1.4.1

    - updated to build with \c qpp from %Qore 1.12.4+

    @section uuid_v_1_4 Version 1.4

    - updated to build with the latest %Qore APIs

    @section uuid_v_1_3 Version 1.3

    - minor build and packaging fixes

    @section uuid_v_1_2 Version 1.2

    - took the following steps to ensure consistent behavior on all platforms:
      - modified the default output (without any flags) to always be a string with lower-case hex digit letters
      - updated implementation to manage case even if the uuid library does not support the uuid_unparse_lower() and uuid_unparse_upper() functions
    - added support for building the module on Windows and with the OSSP UUID library
    - note that UUID generation flags are ignored on Windows

    @section uuid_v_1_1 Version 1.1

    - added the following static method allowing a string UUID to be returned immediately without creating an object:
      - static @ref Qore::UUID::UUID::get(int, int) "UUID::get()"
    - minor corrections were made in the documentation

    @section uuid_v_1_0 Version 1.0
    - initial release
*/
